  "headline": "City of the Sacred Sangam",
  "short_description": "Formerly Allahabad, Prayagraj sits at the Triveni Sangam — the confluence of the Ganga, Yamuna and mythical Saraswati rivers — and hosts the Kumbh Mela.",
  "about": "Prayagraj is one of Hinduism's holiest cities, famed for the Sangam and as the periodic host of the Kumbh Mela, the world's largest religious gathering.\n\nLocated at the confluence of the Ganga and Yamuna rivers in southern Uttar Pradesh.\n\nA centre of literature and politics, home to Allahabad University and the Nehru family's Anand Bhavan.\n\nOne of the four sites of the Kumbh Mela and a major Hindu pilgrimage destination.",
  "history": "An ancient city referenced in Hindu scriptures as Prayag, later renamed Allahabad under Akbar, and a major centre of the Indian independence movement.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Prayagraj Airport (airport)\n- Prayagraj Junction (railway)\n- Zero Road Bus Station (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Hindi, English\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "October to March (Kumbh Mela dates vary by astrological cycle)",
  "ideal_duration_text": "1–2 days",
